@startuml
title Containerized Song Mood Lookup Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 200
left to right direction

' Actors
actor "End User" as EndUser
actor "Operator" as Operator
actor "Data Inspector" as DataInspector

' External dependency
cloud "Genius API\n(External)" as Genius

' Dockerized deployment with separate container services
node "Dockerized Application Stack\n(Docker/Compose network)" as Docker {
  component "React Frontend\n(frontend service)" as Frontend <<container>>
  component "FastAPI Backend\n(backend service)" as Backend <<container>>
  database "Elasticsearch\n(storage service)" as ES <<container>>
  component "Kibana\n(kibana service)" as Kibana <<container>>
}

' Primary interactions
EndUser --> Frontend : HTTP(S)\nBrowser access
Frontend --> Backend : REST/JSON\nSong lookup requests
Backend --> ES : Query/Store\nSong records & mood associations
Kibana --> ES : Connect for data inspection
Backend --> Genius : HTTPS\nSearch missing songs

' Roles accessing Kibana
Operator --> Kibana : Access Kibana UI
DataInspector --> Kibana : Inspect stored data

' Notes on components and constraints
note right of ES
- Stores song records (name, SLink, lyrics, language)
- Stores mood associations (song -> mood)
end note

note top of Backend
- No runtime mood classifier/inference
- Uses Elasticsearch as authoritative store
- Uses Genius API when song not found
end note

note bottom of Docker
Separate container services:
- frontend (React)
- backend (FastAPI)
- elasticsearch
- kibana
end note

note bottom of Frontend
Does not access storage directly
end note

note right of Genius
External dependency; not an internal container service
end note

note as Scope
Project dataset scope: English songs
(No runtime language rejection required)
end note

Scope .. Docker

@enduml